
## Procedure

### Step 1: Create a Jira Project
1. Open https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira.
2. Log in using your Atlassian account.
3. Navigate to Projects/Spaces.
4. Click on Create Project.
5. Select Software Development.
6. Choose the Scrum template.
7. Select the project management type if prompted.
8. Enter Project Name as Online Food Ordering System.
9. Enter Project Key as OFS.
10. Click Create Project.

### Step 2: Create Epics
1. Open the created project.
2. Navigate to Backlog.
3. Open the Epics panel.
4. Click Create Epic.
5. Enter the Epic name and description.
6. Save the Epic.
7. Repeat the process to create the following five Epics:

| Sr. No. | Epic Name |
|---|---|
| 1 | User Management |
| 2 | Restaurant Management |
| 3 | Order Management |
| 4 | Payment Management |
| 5 | Delivery Tracking |

### Step 3: Create User Stories
1. Navigate to Backlog.
2. Click Create.
3. Select issue type as Story.
4. Enter the Summary and Description.
5. Link the Story to its respective Epic.
6. Click Create.
7. Repeat for all eight User Stories.

**User Story 1: Customer Registration**

Epic: User Management

Description: As a customer, I want to register by providing my name, email address and password so that I can create an account and use the food ordering system.

**User Story 2: Customer Login**

Epic: User Management

Description: As a registered customer, I want to log in using my email and password so that I can securely access my account.

**User Story 3: View Restaurants**

Epic: Restaurant Management

Description: As a customer, I want to view the list of available restaurants so that I can choose a restaurant according to my preferences.

**User Story 4: Search Food Items**

Epic: Restaurant Management

Description: As a customer, I want to search for food items by name or category so that I can quickly find the food I want to order.

**User Story 5: Add Items to Cart**

Epic: Order Management

Description: As a customer, I want to add selected food items to my cart so that I can review my order before placing it.

**User Story 6: Place Food Order**

Epic: Order Management

Description: As a customer, I want to place an order after reviewing my cart so that the restaurant can prepare and deliver my food.

**User Story 7: Online Payment**

Epic: Payment Management

Description: As a customer, I want to pay for my food order using an online payment method so that I can complete my purchase securely.

**User Story 8: Track Food Delivery**

Epic: Delivery Tracking

Description: As a customer, I want to track my food delivery status so that I know whether my order is being prepared, dispatched or delivered.

### Step 4: Create Sprint 1
1. Open the Backlog section.
2. Click Create Sprint.
3. A new Sprint section will appear.
4. Move the following three User Stories into Sprint 1:
   - Customer Registration
   - Customer Login
   - View Restaurants
5. Click Start Sprint.
6. Enter the following details:
   - Sprint Name: Sprint 1
   - Duration: 1 Week
   - Sprint Goal: Develop basic customer registration, login and restaurant viewing functionality.
7. Click Start.

### Step 5: Work with Scrum Board
1. Open the Active Sprints or Board section.
2. View the tasks assigned to Sprint 1.
3. Move Customer Registration from To Do to In Progress and then to Done.
4. Move Customer Login from To Do to In Progress.
5. Keep View Restaurants in To Do.
6. Verify the updated task statuses.

**Final Status:**
- Customer Registration – Done
- Customer Login – In Progress
- View Restaurants – To Do

### Step 6: Explore List View
1. Open the Jira project.
2. Click List from the left sidebar.
3. Observe all the created User Stories.
4. Check their issue keys, summaries and statuses.
5. Observe the Assignee, Priority and Issue Type fields if available.
6. Verify the task statuses.

### Step 7: Explore Timeline View
1. Open the Jira project.
2. Click Timeline.
3. Observe all five Epics.
4. Open an Epic to view its details.
5. Set the Start Date and Due Date if available.
6. Save the changes.
7. Observe the visual timeline bars.

Sample schedule for User Management:
- Start Date: 03/11/2026
- Due Date: 10/11/2026

### Step 8: Add Collaborators
1. Open the Jira project.
2. Navigate to Project Settings or Space Settings.
3. Open the People or Access section.
4. Click Add People.
5. Enter the registered email address of a team member.
6. Select an appropriate project role.
7. Click Add.
8. Verify that the collaborator appears in the People list.

### Step 9: Assign Tasks to Team Members
1. Open the Scrum Board or List View.
2. Select a User Story.
3. Open its issue details.
4. Locate the Assignee field.
5. Search for the collaborator's username or email.
6. Select the team member.
7. Save the changes if required.
8. Verify the assigned person.

### Step 10: Understand DevOps Pipeline Integration
Jira can be integrated with GitHub and Jenkins to support software development and delivery.

